# SESS-EARLY: a setting chosen before a session's first prompt reaches its
# log. fx v0.0.16 holds every setting made before the first turn in memory
# and writes them with it (session_manager/session.zig:415-429, :503-539
# @481104fd). The profile is put back between the two launches, so only the
# session's log can say what the first one chose: the resumed footer, and the
# request after the resume, show whether it did.
fx: env FX_AUTO_UPGRADE=0
models p5-session-early-prefs-models.json
gateway p5-session-early-prefs-turns.json
seed p5-session-early-prefs-seed.json
nomodel
wait 3
snap launch
paste /model anthropic/claude-opus-5 high fast
wait 0.4
key Enter
wait 1
snap chosen
type first prompt please
key Enter
wait 3
snap answered
home first-save
keep
type /quit
wait 0.5
key Enter
wait 2
reseed p5-session-early-prefs-seed.json
home reseeded
fx: relaunch --resume-last
xfx: relaunch --resume last
wait 5
snap resumed
type after the resume
key Enter
wait 3
snap continued
home end
gwlog
